		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>This paper presents the submission of NTTSU for the constrained track of the English-Japanese and Japanese-Chinese at the WMT2025 general translation task. For each translation direction, we build translation models from a large language model by combining continual pretraining, supervised fine-tuning, and preference optimization based on the translation quality and adequacy. We finally generate translations via context-aware MBR decoding to maximize translation quality and document-level consistency.</p>
			</abstract>
